 ## 7a. Standard library **[M3]**
 Node's names, so existing habits work:
-- `import { readFileSync, readFileBytesSync, writeFileSync, appendFileSync, existsSync, readdirSync, mkdirSync, rmSync, unlinkSync, statSync, accessSync, renameSync, rename, chmodSync, openSync, writeSync, fsyncSync, fdatasyncSync, closeSync } from "node:fs"` (also `"fs"`, `"std/fs"`): the synchronous API; failures throw `Error` with Node's messages (`ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'x'`). `readdirSync` returns sorted names. `readFileBytesSync` returns the file's `u8[]` (what Node's `readFileSync` gives as a Buffer), and `writeFileSync`/`appendFileSync` take `string | u8[]`. `statSync` returns a `Stats` (`size`, `mtimeMs`, `mode`, `isFile()`, `isDirectory()`); `renameSync(from, to)` is POSIX rename (an existing `to` is replaced in one step) and `rename(from, to, callback)` its callback form; `openSync(path, flags?, mode?)` returns a descriptor (Node's flags: `r`, `r+`, `w`, `wx`, `w+`, `a`, `ax`, `a+`; `r` opens a directory too) for `writeSync`, `fsyncSync`, `fdatasyncSync` and `closeSync`; `writeFileSync(path, data, { mode, flush })` sets a created file's mode and fsyncs with `flush: true`; `chmodSync(path, mode)`. Together they make a durable atomic write: write a temporary file in the same directory with `flush: true`, `renameSync` it over the target, then `fsyncSync` the directory; `accessSync(path, mode?)` takes Node's mode flags (0 exists, 4 read, 2 write, 1 execute).
+- `import { readFileSync, readFileBytesSync, writeFileSync, appendFileSync, existsSync, readdirSync, mkdirSync, rmSync, unlinkSync, statSync, accessSync, renameSync, rename, chmodSync, openSync, writeSync, fsyncSync, fdatasyncSync, closeSync, flockSync } from "node:fs"` (also `"fs"`, `"std/fs"`): the synchronous API; failures throw `Error` with Node's messages (`ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'x'`). `readdirSync` returns sorted names. `readFileBytesSync` returns the file's `u8[]` (what Node's `readFileSync` gives as a Buffer), and `writeFileSync`/`appendFileSync` take `string | u8[]`. `statSync` returns a `Stats` (`size`, `mtimeMs`, `mode`, `isFile()`, `isDirectory()`); `renameSync(from, to)` is POSIX rename (an existing `to` is replaced in one step) and `rename(from, to, callback)` its callback form; `openSync(path, flags?, mode?)` returns a descriptor (Node's flags: `r`, `r+`, `w`, `wx`, `w+`, `a`, `ax`, `a+`; `r` opens a directory too) for `writeSync`, `fsyncSync`, `fdatasyncSync`, `closeSync` and `flockSync(fd, "ex" | "sh" | "un", waitMs?)` (flock(2): `false` when another descriptor held the lock for `waitMs`, 0 tries once; the kernel releases it when the descriptor closes or its process dies); `writeFileSync(path, data, { mode, flush })` sets a created file's mode and fsyncs with `flush: true`; `chmodSync(path, mode)`. Together they make a durable atomic write: write a temporary file in the same directory with `flush: true`, `renameSync` it over the target, then `fsyncSync` the directory; `accessSync(path, mode?)` takes Node's mode flags (0 exists, 4 read, 2 write, 1 execute).
